## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | 5 |
| **High** | 1 |
| **Medium** | 2 |

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** suite. Every public method is called, giving you 95% line coverage, but almost nothing is actually verified. Bugs in price math, search logic, CSV parsing, etc. sail straight to production.

---

### 🔴 Critical

#### 1. Coverage-Touching (Systemic)

The entire suite follows a pattern: call the method, discard the result. 5 of 10 tests have **zero assertions**; the other 5 only assert `IsNotNull` — which passes for any non-null garbage.

---

#### 2. No Assertions — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)

```csharp
// BEFORE — proves only that no exception is thrown
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// AFTER — verify the product is retrievable with correct values
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

---

#### 3. No Assertions — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 33)

```csharp
// BEFORE
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

// AFTER
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

---

#### 4. No Assertions — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 39)

```csharp
// BEFORE
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

// AFTER
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

---

#### 5. No Assertions — `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)

```csharp
// BEFORE
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();

// AFTER
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();
Assert.AreEqual(1, count);
```

---

#### 6. No Assertions — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 69)

This one is especially dangerous — the discount math (`Price * (1 - fraction)`) is never verified.

```csharp
// BEFORE
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);

// AFTER
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
var discounted = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(8.99m, discounted!.Price);  // 9.99 * 0.90
```

---

### 🟠 High

#### 7. Trivial `IsNotNull` Assertions — `GetProduct_Works`, `SearchProducts_Works`, `GetAllProducts_Works`, `ExportToCsv_Works` (lines 25, 46, 55, 77)

`Assert.IsNotNull` only proves the method returned *something*. It will never catch wrong results.

```csharp
// BEFORE (GetProduct_Works)
